for t in trials:lines.append(f"| {t['query']}: {t['question']} | {', '.join(t['chronological_output'])} | {', '.join(t['decision_index_output'])} | A=4; B={t['indexed_entries_considered']} | Same scoped findings |")
lines+=['','The counts are operation counts in this declared lookup, not measured reading time or a claim about model internals. A needs no new indexing work and remains useful for chronological review. B is chosen for these repeated obstacle-based queries because it supplies the same scoped findings while presenting fewer irrelevant candidates in each tested lookup. The decision does not establish an optimal organization for unknown future queries.','','Actual use: the next RLCL input is the source’s “certainty contradicts hope” relation. The confidence-entailment entry returns K3 plus K1. The model carries forward two explicit checks: identify whether certainty is factive or a confidence expression, and identify the exact proposition/time whose uncertainty is at issue. The next record therefore tests C(P,t) against H(Q,u), preserving the P=Q/t=u and P≠Q/t≠u cases separately. This is a performed input classification and is used in 14-rlcl-certainty-hope.md.','','Review: Content comparison finds no lost scope, exception, or provenance among K1–K4. Organization comparison reveals an unresolved trade-off: B’s obstacle terms must be recognized; A remains easier when the user names an application number. The repair is to retain both entry points, with B as the default for the tested obstacle queries. No additional useful distinction was found in these comparisons; no claim is made that none exists.','','Actual mind change: The next source-relation analysis uses the obstacle index and receives the factivity/operand conditions before assigning a relation verdict.','Benefit: The tested lookups return all and only their retained relevant findings with fewer candidate records presented; the following RLCL operation consumes the selected conditions. This is local organization benefit, not another independent substantive keep.','Verdict: KEEP — consolidation organization only; substantive keep count remains four.','Organization: Obstacle-indexed access plus chronological fallback, original records linked, exceptions preserved, multi-entry membership allowed. The next consolidation is due after four more distinct substantive keeps.','Next attempts: Apply the index to the certainty/hope relation; test a query naming an application number; add the next four eligible findings without erasing incompatible scopes; compare a condition-first organization if obstacle recognition fails.']
